# Haikamera — configuration
#
# Easiest path: run with NO key at all. The app boots in DEMO MODE with a canned
# verse, so you can try the whole UI on your phone immediately. (Every photo
# returns the SAME sample haiku — add a key for a real, per-photo poem.)
#
# To go live, add a free key for an open-weight vision model (section 1).

# Copy to .env and run:  node server.js   (the server auto-loads .env)

# 1) Vision model — leave empty for DEMO MODE, or paste a free key.
#    It looks at your photo and writes a short colour-poem (5-7-5 haiku). Your
#    own photo is still the only image shown; no other picture is fetched.
AI_API_KEY=

#    Run MORE THAN ONE provider at once by listing several keys instead. Each is
#    auto-detected from its prefix and tried in the order written, so a Groq key
#    leads (fast, 1,000/day) and OpenRouter free picks up the slack when Groq is
#    busy or out — and vice versa. When one key's day is spent, the server just
#    moves on to the next key instead of giving up.
#
# AI_API_KEYS=gsk_your_groq_key,sk-or-v1-your_openrouter_key
#
#    Note: with several keys, the single-provider overrides below (AI_PROVIDER /
#    AI_BASE_URL / AI_MODEL / AI_FALLBACK_MODELS) are ignored — each key keeps
#    its own provider's defaults, since one model name can't describe two hosts.
#
#    Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint serving an OPEN-WEIGHT vision model works.
#    The provider is auto-detected from your key's prefix (sk-or- → OpenRouter,
#    gsk_ → Groq, nvapi- → NVIDIA, hf_ → Hugging Face), so usually you only need
#    to paste the key. Override with AI_PROVIDER / AI_BASE_URL / AI_MODEL if you
#    want something specific.
#
#    Default: Google Gemma 4 31B on OpenRouter — open-weight, and the best
#    writer of the free set. The shared pool rate-limits it often, so the chain
#    falls through to Gemma 4 26B, then Nemotron 3 Nano Omni and
#    dots-3-note-preview, which answer most dependably (~3s per poem once
#    reasoning is switched off). A 429 costs ~300ms, so leading with Gemma is
#    nearly free.
#
#    Provider       Free tier                          Base URL                             Example open-weight vision model
#    -------------- ---------------------------------- ------------------------------------ ------------------------------------------
#    OpenRouter     20 req/min, 50 req/day, no card    https://openrouter.ai/api/v1            google/gemma-4-31b-it:free
#    Groq           no card, 30 req/min, 1,000/day      https://api.groq.com/openai/v1          qwen/qwen3.8-27b
#    NVIDIA NIM     120+ open-weight models, no card   https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1     meta/llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct
#    Hugging Face   Inference Providers, free tier      https://router.huggingface.co/v1        Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct
#
#    Heads-up on Groq: it retired its Llama 4 vision models in 2026 (Maverick in
#    March, Scout in July) and the suggested replacements are text-only, so for a
#    while a Groq key couldn't read a photo at all. qwen/qwen3.8-27b is its one
#    multimodal model now — and it's a *preview* model, so expect it to move.
#
#    Higher-quality (paid) upgrades on OpenRouter, same one-line swap. These are
#    absurdly cheap per poem (a 512px frame is ~330 input tokens):
#      inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-vl         — $0.021/M in  ≈ $0.000013 a poem
#      qwen/qwen3.7-flash                    — $0.030/M in
#      google/gemini-2.5-flash               — the best value in the mid range
#      qwen/qwen3-vl-235b-a22b-instruct      — best visual grounding

#    Optional: force a provider/model instead of auto-detecting from the key.
# AI_PROVIDER=openrouter
# AI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# AI_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free

#    Comma-separated backups, tried in order if the primary errors, is
#    rate-limited, or is withdrawn. Empty disables fallbacks. Defaults per
#    provider (the OpenRouter default is the chain below); override to change.
# AI_FALLBACK_MODELS=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free,nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning:free,dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free
#
#    Output cap per request. Nearly every free vision model is a *reasoning*
#    model, so this has to leave room for the thinking before the JSON. With
#    reasoning switched off (below) the reply is ~90 tokens and this is slack.
# AI_MAX_TOKENS=2000
#
#    Reasoning models think before they answer. For a three-line haiku that is
#    pure waste: switching it off took a request from ~22s to ~3s and stopped
#    the thinking from eating the output budget (which is what used to leave an
#    empty reply and hand you the fallback verse). Default: off for OpenRouter,
#    left alone everywhere else (other hosts spell it differently).
# AI_REASONING=off
#
#    Reliability note: a free OpenRouter account is capped at 20 requests per
#    MINUTE and 50 requests per DAY on ":free" models (a one-off $10 credit
#    raises the day to 1,000; the per-minute cap stays). When the day's quota is
#    spent, every free model returns 429. With a single key that means the app
#    says so plainly rather than showing a canned poem (it resets daily); add a
#    second key with AI_API_KEYS and it will route around the dead one instead.
#    Note that each poem can spend several requests (one per model attempt), so
#    the free tier is for trying the app, not for sharing it. For real use, add
#    a Groq key (1,000/day free, no card) or a little OpenRouter credit on a
#    paid model.

#    Optional attribution headers sent to OpenRouter (ignored by other hosts).
AI_APP_TITLE=Haikamera
AI_APP_URL=https://github.com/safeamiiir/haikamera

# 2) Port for the local server (binds to all interfaces so your phone can reach it).
PORT=8787
